{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["vite/client"]
  },
  // `include` deliberately stays ["src"] — it is NOT widened to
  // ../apps/web/src/aftersign (#836, acceptance criterion 2, "documented
  // as not typechecked" branch). That tree was authored without ever
  // running under this tsconfig's strict flags (strict / noUnusedLocals /
  // noUnusedParameters, `types: ["vite/client"]` only), so widening the
  // include turns `typecheck:aftersign` — a BLOCKING ci.yml step — red on
  // latent errors across ~25 files that no PR can triage in one diff
  // (this exact failure killed PR #837's first attempts, and #851's first
  // attempt at #846's option-1 path — vitest imports resolve now, but the
  // ~25 latent errors underneath do not, so widening still turns the
  // blocking gate red).
  //
  // BURN-DOWN (#843, #846): the ~25 files are typechecked instead by
  // `aftersign/tsconfig.apps-web.json`, wired via
  // `npm run typecheck:aftersign:apps-web` and run as a non-blocking
  // step (`continue-on-error: true`) in ci.yml's aftersign lane. As
  // errors are fixed file-by-file, the burn-down step will land green
  // on its own; when it does, it flips to blocking (drop
  // `continue-on-error`) and the sibling `include` can be merged back
  // into this one — see the sibling's header comment.
  //
  // Status of apps/web/src/aftersign/ until then:
  //   - RUNTIME: executed by vitest via `test:unit:aftersign`
  //     (package.json / ci.yml aftersign lane).
  //   - TYPECHECK: best-effort blocking + burn-down non-blocking. Files
  //     that aftersign/src imports directly (e.g. recognitionFeedback.ts
  //     via recognitionBeat.ts) ARE transitively typechecked here under
  //     the blocking gate; the rest are typechecked under the sibling
  //     burn-down config, whose failures currently do not gate merges.
  //     Type-level pins (`satisfies`, Record<> alignment tables) in
  //     un-imported files are visible in the burn-down log — see
  //     aftersign/README.md.
  // Do NOT add `**/*.test.ts` to `exclude`: aftersign/src/*.test.ts are
  // plain-TS assertion runners that are deliberately typechecked by this
  // config (see aftersign/src/packetIntentContract.test.ts header).
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "../dist-aftersign", "e2e", "playwright.config.ts", "vite.config.ts"]
}
